(tmp file removed afterwards; the gate re-passes)

### M11 — assertion logic driven with the old vacuous capture (rc=0):
The new if-guard captures the real exit code; the assertion compares it
against 2. With rc=0 (what the old `|| true` always produced) the check
reports FAIL; with the real run rc=2 and the gate PASSes.

### M16a — header-absence branch driven live:
- Origin present + key:  cors_header=Access-Control-Allow-Origin: https://evil.example -> PASS branch
- No Origin:            FAIL branch: no Access-Control-Allow-Origin header emitted

